#### 1. Introduction

The aim of this study is to investigate the effect of the use of a mobile application on the quality of life of patients with chronic diseases. The study will be conducted in the city of London, UK, and will involve a total of 100 participants. The participants will be divided into two groups: a control group and an intervention group. The control group will receive standard care, while the intervention group will receive standard care plus access to a mobile application designed to improve the quality of life of patients with chronic diseases. The study will be conducted over a period of six months, and participants will be asked to complete questionnaires at the beginning and end of the study to assess their quality of life.

The study will use a randomized controlled trial design, with participants randomly assigned to either the control or intervention group. The mobile application will be designed to provide patients with information and tools to manage their chronic disease, including tracking their symptoms, medication adherence, and lifestyle changes. The application will also provide patients with access to a community of other patients with chronic diseases, allowing them to connect and share experiences.

The study will be conducted in collaboration with healthcare providers in London, who will provide participants with standard care and support throughout the study. The study will also involve the use of wearable technology, such as fitness trackers and smartwatches, to collect data on participants' physical activity levels and other health metrics.

The study aims to contribute to the growing body of research on the use of mobile applications in improving the quality of life of patients with chronic diseases. By investigating the effectiveness of a mobile application in improving quality of life, the study hopes to provide insights into the potential benefits of using mobile technology in healthcare.

#### 2. Background

Chronic diseases are a major public health concern, affecting millions of people worldwide. These diseases include conditions such as diabetes, heart disease, and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD), among others. Chronic diseases are characterized by long-term health problems that require ongoing management and care. Patients with chronic diseases often experience a range of negative impacts on their quality of life, including reduced physical and mental health, social isolation, and reduced ability to work or engage in activities they enjoy.

Mobile applications have the potential to improve the quality of life of patients with chronic diseases. These applications can provide patients with access to information and tools to manage their condition, connect with other patients, and receive support from healthcare providers. Mobile applications can also be used to collect data on patients' health metrics, allowing healthcare providers to monitor patients' progress and adjust treatment plans accordingly.

Despite the potential benefits of mobile applications in improving the quality of life of patients with chronic diseases, there is limited research on the effectiveness of these applications. Many studies have focused on the use of mobile applications in improving specific health outcomes, such as medication adherence or physical activity levels. However, there is a need for more research on the broader impact of mobile applications on quality of life.

#### 3. Methodology

The study will use a randomized controlled trial design, with participants randomly assigned to either the control or intervention group. The study will be conducted over a period of six months, with participants completing questionnaires at the beginning and end of the study to assess their quality of life.

