#### 4. Expected outcomes

The study aims to investigate the effect of the use of a mobile application on the quality of life of patients with chronic diseases. The study will assess participants' quality of life using standardized questionnaires, such as the Short Form-36 (SF-36) and the EuroQol-5D (EQ-5D). The study will also collect data on participants' physical activity levels, medication adherence, and other health metrics using wearable technology.

The study aims to achieve the following outcomes:

1. To investigate the effect of the use of a mobile application on the quality of life of patients with chronic diseases.

2. To compare the quality of life of participants in the control group and intervention group at the end of the study.

3. To investigate the impact of the mobile application on medication adherence, physical activity levels, and other health metrics.

4. To explore the experiences of participants using the mobile application and identify any barriers or facilitators to using the application.

#### 5. Conclusion

